Bible texts
  The application only ships Bible translations that are in the public
  domain. They are not covered by the AGPL and remain free for anyone to use:

  - Louis Segond 1910 (French) - public domain ("Cette Bible est dans le
    domaine public"). Source: eBible.org, "fraLSG", VPL edition
    (https://ebible.org/find/details.php?id=fraLSG).
    Stored in packages/bible-data/data/lsg1910.
  - King James Version, 1769 standard text (English) - public domain,
    except in the United Kingdom where printing it is subject to Crown
    rights (letters patent). Source: eBible.org, "eng-kjv2006", VPL
    edition, without Strong's numbers
    (https://ebible.org/find/details.php?id=eng-kjv2006).
    Stored in packages/bible-data/data/kjv.
  - Berean Standard Bible (English) - public domain. Source: eBible.org,
    "engbsb", VPL edition (https://ebible.org/find/details.php?id=engbsb).
    Stored in packages/bible-data/data/bsb.
  - World English Bible (English) - public domain. Source: eBible.org,
    "engwebp", VPL edition (https://ebible.org/find/details.php?id=engwebp).
    Stored in packages/bible-data/data/web.

  The texts are converted, not edited, by
  packages/bible-data/scripts/import-ebible.ts (one JSON file per chapter,
  Unicode normalization and spacing only). Copyrighted modern translations
  are never included; the application only links to external readers
  (e.g. YouVersion) for them.

Datasets
  Bible structure data (books, chapters, verse counts) and reading orders
  (e.g. chronological order) included in this repository are listed below
  with their source and license as they are added.

  - Verse counts per chapter (packages/core/src/bible/verse-counts.ts):
    King James Version versification (1769 text, public domain), i.e. 66
    books, 1,189 chapters and 31,102 verses. They are facts counted from
    the public-domain text and were checked chapter by chapter against a
    digital edition of the KJV.

  - Book names and abbreviations (packages/core/src/bible/books.ts): OSIS
    book identifiers (public standard, https://crosswire.org/osis), Louis
    Segond 1910 names in French and King James Version names in English.

  - Chronological reading order (packages/core/src/plans/
    chronological-order.ts): compiled by the Bible Plan contributors from
    the historical setting given by the biblical text itself (psalm titles,
    reigns named by the prophets, journeys in Acts). It is an original work
    of this project, licensed under the AGPL like the code. It does not
    reproduce any published chronological plan; the dates of several books
    are debated, so the order is approximate.

  - M'Cheyne's Calendar for Daily Readings (Robert Murray M'Cheyne, 1842):
    public domain. The template follows its structure (four readings a day,
    the Old Testament once, the New Testament and the Psalms twice); the
    day-by-day split is computed by this project's plan generator.

  - Country codes (ISO 3166-1 alpha-2) and flags: flag-icons
    (https://github.com/lipis/flag-icons), MIT License, Copyright (c) 2013
    Panayiotis Lipiridis. Country names are generated at runtime by
    Intl.DisplayNames (Unicode CLDR data).

